hadiths[17]{hadithnumber,text}:
"221","Qabisa ibn Burma al-Asadi said, \I was with the Messenger of Allah"
"222","Harmala ibn 'Abdullah went to the Prophet, may Allah bless him\nand grant him peace, and stayed with him until the Prophet, may Allah bless\nhim and grant him peace, until the Prophet, may Allah bless him and grant\nhim peace, recognised him. He said, \When we set out"
"223","Salman said, \The people of correctness in this world are the people\nof correctness in the Next World.\"""""
"224","Jabir ibn 'Abdullah reported that the Messenger of Allah, may Allah\nbless him and grant him peace, said, \Every correct action is sadaqa.\"""""
"225","Abu Musa reported that the Prophet, may Allah bless him and grant\nhim peace, said, \Every Muslim must give sadaqa.\"" They said"
"226","Musaddad narrated to us, saying: Yahya narrated to us, from Hisham ibn Urwah, who said: My father narrated to me, that Abu Murawh al-Ghifari informed him, that Abu Dharr informed him, that he asked the Messenger of Allah ﷺ: ""Which deed is best?"" He said: ""Faith in Allah and jihad in His path."" He said: ""Then which slaves are best to free?"" He said: ""The most expensive in price and the most precious to their people."" He said: ""What if I cannot do that?"" He said: ""Help a craftsman or make something for an unskilled person."" He said: ""What if I cannot do that?"" He said: ""Refrain from harming people, for that is a charity you give on behalf of yourself."""
"227","Here is the translated text in English:Abu al-Nu'man narrated to us, saying: Mahdi bin Maimun narrated to me, from Wasil, the mawla of Abu 'Uyaynah, from Yahya bin 'Aqil, from Yahya bin Ya'mur, from Abu al-Aswad ad-Dili, from Abu Zarr, who said: It was said: O Messenger of Allah, the people of the deserts have been given their rewards, they pray as we pray, they fast as we fast, and they give in charity with the wealth they have. He said: Is it not that Allah has made for you what you give in charity? Indeed, every act of worship and every praise is charity, and the wealth of one of you is charity. It was said: Is the charity in his hunger? He said: If he were to place it in the Haram, would it not be a burden upon him? That is, if he were to place it in the Halal, he would have a reward."
"228","Abu Barza al-Aslami said, \I said"
"229","Abu Hurayra reported that the Prophet, may Allah bless him and\ngrant him peace, said, \A man came across a thorn in the road and said"
"230","Abu Dharr reported that the Messenger of Allah, may Allah bless\nhim and grant him peace, said, \I was shown the actions of my Community\n- both good and evil - and I found that one of their good actions\nis removing harmful things from the road"
"231","'Abdullah ibn al-Khatami reported that the Messenger of Allah,\nmay Allah bless him and grant him peace, said, \Every act of kindness is\nsadaqa.\"""""
"232","He narrated to us Sa'id bin Sulayman, who said: Mubarak narrated to us, from Thabit, from Anas, who said: The Prophet (peace be upon him) would say when something was brought to him: ""Take it to Fulanah, for she is the friend of Khadijah. Take it to Fulanah's house, for she loves Khadijah."""
"233","Muhammad ibn Kathir narrated to us, he said: Sufyan informed us, from Abu Malik al-Ashja'i, from Rib'i, from Hudhayfah, may Allah be pleased with him, who said: Your Prophet, peace be upon him, said: Every act of kindness is charity."
"234","'Amr ibn Qurra al-Kindi said, \My father offered his sister in\nmarriage to Salman. He refused and then married a mawla of his called Buqayra.\nAbu Qurra heard that there were bad feelings between Hudhayfa and Salman.\nHe went to talk to him (Salman) about this. He was told that he was in\na vegetable garden which belonged to him and went and met him there. Salman\nhad a sack of vegetables. He put his stick in the knot of the sack and\nput it on his shoulder. Abu Qurra asked"
"235","Here is the translated text in English:Hadith:Ibn Abi Shaybah narrated to us, saying: Yahya bin Isa narrated to us, from Al-A'mash, from Habib, from Sa'id bin Jubayr, from Ibn Abbas, who said: Omar, may Allah be pleased with him, said: ""Let us go out to the land of our people."" So we went out, and I was with Ubayy bin Ka'b in the rear of the people, and a cloud overshadowed us, and Ubayy said: ""O Allah, turn away from us this cloud."" So we caught up with them, and their camels had been beset, and they said: ""What has befallen you that has befallen us?"" I said: ""It is because he called upon Allah, the Exalted, to turn away from us this cloud,"" and Omar said: ""Did you not call upon Allah for us along with you?"""
"236","Abu Salama said, \We went to Abu Sa'id al-Khudri with a friend.\nI said"
"237","Here is the translated text in English:

Mohammed bin Salam narrated to us, saying: Mohammed bin al-Fudayl bin Ghazwan narrated to us, from Mughira, from Umm Musa, who said: I heard Ali (peace be upon him) say: The Prophet (peace be upon him) ordered Abdullah bin Mas'ud to ascend a tree and bring something from it. His companions looked at the back of Abdullah and laughed at the shape of his back, so the Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him) said: What are you laughing at? The leg of Abdullah is heavier in the balance than Uhud."
